# Phase 1: NuttX (icicle:nsh) alone on U54 hart 1, the flight-control core in the paper.
# E51 (bootloader) and U54 harts 2-4 (future Linux) are held halted; the ELF is loaded straight into DDR
# instead of going through HSS.
#
# Build:  sw/build-nuttx.sh
# Run:    sim/phase1/run.sh [gui|headless]     (the script does not call `start`; run.sh does)
# NSH:    GUI analyzer window, or telnet localhost $nshport, default 33457 (also logged to logs/nuttx-mmuart1.log)
# Check:  sim/phase1/check-one-core.sh

$nuttx?=$ORIGIN/../../sw/nuttx/nuttx
$nshport?=33457
$uartlog?=$ORIGIN/logs/nuttx-mmuart1.log

using sysbus
mach create "uav"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/polarfire-soc.repl

# Errors only; the PolarFire model is very chatty at WARNING level.
logLevel 3

# Expect 187 "plic: Trying to complete irq N" errors at boot: NuttX's PLIC init (mpfs_plic.c, "Complete
# possibly claimed IRQs ... in case of warm reboot") writes every IRQ number to the claim/complete register.
# Real hardware ignores completes for unclaimed IRQs. They can't be muted per peripheral: ERROR (3) is
# Renode's highest log level.

e51 IsHalted true
u54_2 IsHalted true
u54_3 IsHalted true
u54_4 IsHalted true

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $nuttx false u54_1
"""
runMacro $reset

mmuart1 CreateFileBackend $uartlog true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $nshport "nsh" false
connector Connect mmuart1 nsh
